1
00:00:11,886 --> 00:00:13,346
It's not that cold and…

2
00:00:13,930 --> 00:00:14,764
What's going on?

3
00:00:15,932 --> 00:00:16,850
A ghost?

4
00:00:21,062 --> 00:00:22,564
Who turned them off?

5
00:00:22,647 --> 00:00:23,481
A SUDDEN BLACKOUT?

6
00:00:24,149 --> 00:00:24,983
10 MINUTES EARLIER

7
00:00:25,066 --> 00:00:26,735
It's so hot. I can't stay here.

8
00:00:26,818 --> 00:00:27,861
Gosh, it's too hot.

9
00:00:27,944 --> 00:00:29,154
KIAN RUNS AWAY FROM THE HEAT

10
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:31,573
It's already 10:00 p.m.?
I should turn a light off.

11
00:00:33,074 --> 00:00:34,701
THE SWITCHES ARE 3.5 M HIGH

12
00:00:34,784 --> 00:00:35,618
KITCHEN
LIVING ROOM

13
00:00:35,702 --> 00:00:37,871
TARGET
THE LIVING ROOM LIGHT SWITCH

14
00:00:41,791 --> 00:00:42,625
Darn it!

15
00:00:56,222 --> 00:00:57,640
Was it this hard to turn them off?

16
00:00:59,934 --> 00:01:02,812
Geez, every single thing.

17
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:04,314
Nothing's easy to do.

18
00:01:05,398 --> 00:01:07,233
What on earth am I doing?

19
00:01:08,568 --> 00:01:09,819
This is so inconvenient!

20
00:01:11,446 --> 00:01:12,280
Focus.

21
00:01:14,949 --> 00:01:16,701
What? I turned them all off.

22
00:01:18,369 --> 00:01:19,662
ALL LIGHTS ARE TURNED OFF NOW

23
00:01:19,746 --> 00:01:20,872
This wasn't what I wanted.

24
00:01:22,999 --> 00:01:24,084
I need to turn one on.

25
00:01:25,710 --> 00:01:27,545
No, it's not a blackout.

26
00:01:27,629 --> 00:01:29,255
- I think Boss turned it off.
- Really?

27
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:31,132
- They're all off.
- I know.

28
00:01:31,216 --> 00:01:32,842
- One will be on soon.
- Let's wait.

29
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:36,930
BUT HE'S NOT TURNING THEM BACK ON?

30
00:01:40,141 --> 00:01:44,103
FUMBLING WITH SOMETHING IN THE DARK

31
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,274
HE INVENTED A TOOL?

32
00:01:51,110 --> 00:01:52,403
There we go.

33
00:01:52,487 --> 00:01:53,488
Okay.

34
00:01:54,197 --> 00:01:55,824
If you want beer, come here.

35
00:01:55,907 --> 00:01:56,741
Okay!

36
00:01:56,825 --> 00:01:57,659
Cheers.

37
00:01:57,742 --> 00:01:59,160
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

38
00:01:59,244 --> 00:02:01,246
- Goodness.
- Cheers.

39
00:02:07,794 --> 00:02:08,628
That's nice.

40
00:02:08,711 --> 00:02:09,546
This is so nice.

41
00:02:09,629 --> 00:02:10,547
I was so thirsty.

42
00:02:10,630 --> 00:02:12,340
You're not puffy at all now.

43
00:02:12,423 --> 00:02:14,676
The sauna was so nice.
I feel less tired today.

44
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:15,718
BEFORE, AFTER

45
00:02:15,802 --> 00:02:16,761
I feel so good now.

46
00:02:17,345 --> 00:02:18,680
The puffiness is all gone.

47
00:02:18,763 --> 00:02:20,849
- The dinner went well too.
- Right.

48
00:02:23,309 --> 00:02:24,310
Okay, cheers.

49
00:02:24,394 --> 00:02:25,728
Cheers.

50
00:02:29,899 --> 00:02:31,067
Very nice.

51
00:02:31,151 --> 00:02:32,402
Cheers.

52
00:02:34,195 --> 00:02:35,697
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

53
00:02:35,780 --> 00:02:37,073
This is so nice.

54
00:02:39,742 --> 00:02:40,743
I'll turn the lights off.

55
00:02:40,827 --> 00:02:43,913
You can go to bed
or drink and talk more if you want.

56
00:02:44,622 --> 00:02:45,540
Are you okay, Zuha?

57
00:02:45,623 --> 00:02:47,458
- Yes.
- You're lasting a long time.

58
00:02:47,542 --> 00:02:49,294
Of course. We're in it together.

59
00:02:49,377 --> 00:02:52,213
By the way, how are you finding it here?

60
00:02:53,673 --> 00:02:56,843
It's… It's difficult
because I haven't done this before.

61
00:02:57,510 --> 00:03:02,056
Meeting strangers like this
is something I haven't done much before.

62
00:03:02,974 --> 00:03:03,808
Isn't it tough?

63
00:03:03,892 --> 00:03:05,018
But it's fun.

64
00:03:05,101 --> 00:03:08,146
Plus, you're trying something new here.

65
00:03:08,229 --> 00:03:09,314
That's not easy.

66
00:03:12,108 --> 00:03:15,111
I mean, it's not just you,
it's hard for everyone.

67
00:03:16,529 --> 00:03:17,572
It's also fun, isn't it?

68
00:03:18,072 --> 00:03:19,908
- It is. I'm about to cry.
- She's crying.

69
00:03:19,991 --> 00:03:20,825
It's tough.

70
00:03:20,909 --> 00:03:21,743
CHOKING UP

71
00:03:21,826 --> 00:03:22,827
It's also fun, right?

72
00:03:22,911 --> 00:03:24,996
- It's fun. It is, but…
- Yeah.

73
00:03:25,079 --> 00:03:26,456
It's tough.

74
00:03:30,668 --> 00:03:32,128
It's tough.

75
00:03:36,341 --> 00:03:37,800
She says it's tough.

76
00:03:38,551 --> 00:03:40,511
What do you find tough, Zuha?

77
00:03:43,598 --> 00:03:47,810
Well, it's quite hard for me
to join conversations.

78
00:03:47,894 --> 00:03:49,479
Conversations? I thought so.

79
00:03:49,562 --> 00:03:51,564
I think it's because of the language.

80
00:03:51,648 --> 00:03:52,774
Her Korean's good.

81
00:03:52,857 --> 00:03:55,818
It is, but I think she's still cautious.

82
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:57,403
I mean, her Korean's good,

83
00:03:57,487 --> 00:03:59,864
but I think her personality is…

84
00:03:59,948 --> 00:04:00,949
- Right.
- Introverted.

85
00:04:01,032 --> 00:04:03,201
Yeah, her Korean's real good though.

86
00:04:05,245 --> 00:04:07,413
<i>Up until the third day,</i>

87
00:04:07,497 --> 00:04:08,581
it felt so awkward.

88
00:04:08,665 --> 00:04:12,126
It was my first time
meeting strangers like that,

89
00:04:12,210 --> 00:04:13,836
so it felt so new to me.

90
00:04:13,920 --> 00:04:16,089
- You feel awkward?
- A bit.

91
00:04:16,172 --> 00:04:17,840
- Like that? Oh, I see.
- Yes.

92
00:04:17,924 --> 00:04:18,883
I get it now.

93
00:04:23,429 --> 00:04:24,514
Hey, Zuha.

94
00:04:24,597 --> 00:04:25,640
- Yes?
- What are you doing?

95
00:04:26,266 --> 00:04:27,267
I'm bored.

96
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:28,184
Come on over.

97
00:04:29,185 --> 00:04:30,311
Can I?

98
00:04:30,395 --> 00:04:31,271
Why didn't you come?

99
00:04:31,938 --> 00:04:36,234
<i>I was still not sure</i>
<i>what kind of role I should play</i>

100
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:37,902
at that time,

101
00:04:37,986 --> 00:04:39,904
so when they brought that up,

102
00:04:39,988 --> 00:04:42,073
I think that's why I teared up.

103
00:04:42,156 --> 00:04:43,074
So it's tougher.

104
00:04:44,325 --> 00:04:45,994
But you don't show it.

105
00:04:46,077 --> 00:04:48,371
So you should open yourself up more.

106
00:04:50,748 --> 00:04:52,875
People are used to seeing me around.

107
00:04:52,959 --> 00:04:55,295
But people rarely have
the chance to meet you.

108
00:04:55,378 --> 00:04:56,546
- Right?
- It's rare.

109
00:04:56,629 --> 00:04:59,257
Yeah, so you should do
whatever you feel like doing.

110
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,050
Since you're the youngest,

111
00:05:01,134 --> 00:05:03,261
I'm sure it's not easy to approach others.

112
00:05:03,344 --> 00:05:05,179
But don't explain everything to her.

113
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:07,307
- Why not?
- Just let her do what she wants to do.

114
00:05:07,390 --> 00:05:08,850
If you explain, she can't do it.

115
00:05:08,933 --> 00:05:10,476
PUZZLED

116
00:05:10,560 --> 00:05:12,228
HE WANTED TO CONSOLE HER, BUT…

117
00:05:12,312 --> 00:05:13,229
Just ignore them.

118
00:05:13,313 --> 00:05:14,230
GONE OFF THE PATH NOW

119
00:05:14,314 --> 00:05:16,149
But that's not easy for someone like her.

120
00:05:16,232 --> 00:05:17,442
This show's for you!

121
00:05:17,525 --> 00:05:18,443
HIS RAISED VOICE

122
00:05:18,526 --> 00:05:20,361
MAKES HER CRY EVEN MORE

123
00:05:20,445 --> 00:05:21,529
Why are you making her cry?

124
00:05:21,612 --> 00:05:22,905
No, no.

125
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:24,240
Hey.

126
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:25,158
I…

127
00:05:25,241 --> 00:05:26,784
I cried too, you know.

128
00:05:27,660 --> 00:05:28,828
When did you cry?

129
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:30,997
I cried too during Season 1.

130
00:05:31,581 --> 00:05:33,166
But it is tough though.

131
00:05:33,249 --> 00:05:34,792
During the day, I was also…

132
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:37,337
I didn't know what to do today either.

133
00:05:37,920 --> 00:05:38,755
Tomorrow,

134
00:05:39,505 --> 00:05:42,300
let's talk it over, Zuha.

135
00:05:42,383 --> 00:05:44,969
But do I give you a hard time…

136
00:05:45,553 --> 00:05:46,763
No, let's talk tomorrow.

137
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:47,680
No.

138
00:05:47,764 --> 00:05:50,016
I was worried
I might be giving you a hard time.

139
00:05:50,099 --> 00:05:51,434
No, definitely not.

140
00:05:52,602 --> 00:05:53,978
To me, you are…

141
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:55,271
I'm very grateful.

142
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:59,192
Don't feel that way.
You have nothing to be sorry about.

143
00:05:59,901 --> 00:06:02,612
We're grateful that you joined us.
I mean it.

144
00:06:04,822 --> 00:06:06,199
- Sorry.
- Did you fart?

145
00:06:06,282 --> 00:06:09,118
I'm sorry. I let out a little gas.

146
00:06:11,079 --> 00:06:12,497
So that's what the sound was.

147
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:16,918
- I wondered what it was.
- It won't smell though.

148
00:06:17,418 --> 00:06:19,253
- Damn it.
- I thought only I heard it.

149
00:06:19,796 --> 00:06:22,507
I was trying hard to hold it in,
but a little came out.

150
00:06:22,590 --> 00:06:23,424
I'M SORRY

151
00:06:25,009 --> 00:06:26,344
Let's go to bed now.

152
00:06:27,637 --> 00:06:28,679
Are you okay?

153
00:06:28,763 --> 00:06:29,847
You'll get puffy eyes.

154
00:06:29,931 --> 00:06:31,516
They're so puffy already.

155
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:32,517
It's crazy.

156
00:06:33,142 --> 00:06:34,352
I hope it's not bad tomorrow.

157
00:06:34,435 --> 00:06:35,603
Thank you.

158
00:06:35,686 --> 00:06:36,687
It's all right.

159
00:06:38,439 --> 00:06:40,441
SOFA, FRIDGE

160
00:06:40,525 --> 00:06:41,442
Good night.

161
00:06:41,943 --> 00:06:46,239
WINDOWSILL

162
00:06:46,322 --> 00:06:48,908
TV CABINET

163
00:06:51,911 --> 00:06:55,456
RAMYEON BOXES

164
00:06:55,540 --> 00:06:57,542
BOSS SLEEPS IN THE KARAOKE ROOM

165
00:06:57,625 --> 00:07:00,294
HANGERS
LIVING ROOM

166
00:07:00,378 --> 00:07:02,171
I hope it snows a bunch.

167
00:07:05,174 --> 00:07:07,510
2:00 A.M.

168
00:07:14,809 --> 00:07:17,520
DAY 4

169
00:07:36,706 --> 00:07:40,042
KIAN'S B&B

170
00:07:42,462 --> 00:07:43,421
It's so white.

171
00:07:43,504 --> 00:07:44,630
IT'S WHITE EVERYWHERE

172
00:07:52,263 --> 00:07:55,975
7:00 A.M.

173
00:07:56,058 --> 00:07:57,226
It's beautiful.

174
00:07:57,310 --> 00:07:59,687
KIAN'S B&B

175
00:07:59,770 --> 00:08:00,855
There's a bench.

176
00:08:03,649 --> 00:08:05,401
Come quickly to help me, Lord.

177
00:08:05,485 --> 00:08:07,236
MORNING PRAYERS AT A SNOWY KIAN'S B&B

178
00:08:10,114 --> 00:08:13,242
JUN-HO GETS UP

179
00:08:14,160 --> 00:08:17,997
ZUHA GETS UP

180
00:08:28,341 --> 00:08:29,383
He's awake.

181
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:30,301
GI-PYO'S UP

182
00:08:34,764 --> 00:08:35,806
Wake up.

183
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:40,353
GROANING

184
00:08:43,105 --> 00:08:45,608
THE BOSS GETS UP

185
00:09:09,048 --> 00:09:14,387
MORNING EXERCISE

186
00:09:40,079 --> 00:09:44,500
MORNING EXERCISE ENDS

187
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,168
Jin-an, do you need sunscreen?

188
00:09:46,252 --> 00:09:48,337
No, we'll get wet anyway when we surf.

189
00:09:48,421 --> 00:09:49,630
I'll bring one.

190
00:09:49,714 --> 00:09:51,132
Thank you.

191
00:09:51,215 --> 00:09:53,259
- And you're going with them, Jun-ho?
- Yes.

192
00:09:53,342 --> 00:09:55,595
After surfing,
we'll go skiing and snowboarding.

193
00:09:56,178 --> 00:09:57,096
Are you leaving now?

194
00:09:57,179 --> 00:09:58,514
Yeah. Today's your last day.

195
00:09:58,598 --> 00:09:59,432
Yeah, last day.

196
00:09:59,515 --> 00:10:00,850
Yes.

197
00:10:00,933 --> 00:10:02,476
- See you again.
- See you.

198
00:10:02,560 --> 00:10:04,645
SAYING GOODBYE TO THOSE CHECKING OUT TODAY

199
00:10:04,729 --> 00:10:06,063
Goodbye, Father. I'll miss you.

200
00:10:06,147 --> 00:10:07,315
My brother.

201
00:10:07,398 --> 00:10:08,232
We'll get going.

202
00:10:08,316 --> 00:10:09,233
- See you later.
- Bye.

203
00:10:09,317 --> 00:10:10,568
- See you.
- See you.

204
00:10:10,651 --> 00:10:11,485
Be safe.

205
00:10:11,569 --> 00:10:13,571
9:30 A.M.
LUGE TEAM & JUN-HO GO OUT

206
00:10:16,198 --> 00:10:18,659
Checkout is at 11:00 a.m.

207
00:10:18,743 --> 00:10:20,786
Well, let's say goodbye to them.

208
00:10:20,870 --> 00:10:21,954
All right.

209
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:28,544
Does Zuha seem okay?

210
00:10:28,628 --> 00:10:30,421
WORRIED

211
00:10:30,504 --> 00:10:31,422
Did it bother you?

212
00:10:31,505 --> 00:10:32,673
It's bothering you, isn't it?

213
00:10:32,757 --> 00:10:34,925
Well, it seemed like
it's been really tough for her.

214
00:10:35,009 --> 00:10:36,510
BOSS IS WORRIED ABOUT ZUHA

215
00:10:36,594 --> 00:10:37,678
I feel bad.

216
00:10:43,726 --> 00:10:44,977
What do I do?

217
00:10:45,978 --> 00:10:47,772
SHE'S WORRIED TOO

218
00:10:53,069 --> 00:10:54,320
- Are you okay?
- Yes.

219
00:10:57,573 --> 00:11:00,409
I think we should have a chat later
with them like yesterday.

220
00:11:00,493 --> 00:11:03,120
Yes, sounds good. Let's do it.

221
00:11:03,204 --> 00:11:05,581
MEANWHILE, THE GUESTS GET READY

222
00:11:05,665 --> 00:11:06,499
TO CHECK OUT

223
00:11:06,582 --> 00:11:09,377
It's a T-shirt,
so I should fold it like one.

224
00:11:13,214 --> 00:11:15,675
Once we go back home,
we have to return to work.

225
00:11:15,758 --> 00:11:18,302
Yeah, I don't even want to think about it.

226
00:11:20,888 --> 00:11:23,140
How did we even bring all this stuff here?

227
00:11:23,224 --> 00:11:24,392
This is so much.

228
00:11:24,475 --> 00:11:25,810
How can we pack all of this up?

229
00:11:25,893 --> 00:11:27,019
We have to.

230
00:11:27,103 --> 00:11:29,939
WE HAVE TO PACK TO GO HOME

231
00:11:33,943 --> 00:11:34,777
There we go.

232
00:11:36,278 --> 00:11:38,364
- It's already 10:30 a.m.
- Right.

233
00:11:38,447 --> 00:11:39,865
We're leaving soon.

234
00:11:39,949 --> 00:11:42,368
Before you check out and leave,

235
00:11:42,451 --> 00:11:45,621
if there's an employee you'd like to
talk to for the last time…

236
00:11:45,704 --> 00:11:46,539
- It's time.
- Yes.

237
00:11:46,622 --> 00:11:48,082
CHECKOUT TALK
WITH CHOSEN STAFF

238
00:11:48,165 --> 00:11:50,042
We'll humbly accept the results.

239
00:11:51,335 --> 00:11:53,421
SHUFFLES BACK

240
00:11:53,504 --> 00:11:54,338
What?

241
00:11:54,422 --> 00:11:56,632
This wasn't what we planned to do.

242
00:11:56,715 --> 00:11:57,550
Four-on-four.

243
00:11:57,633 --> 00:11:59,927
This isn't some reality dating show.

244
00:12:00,010 --> 00:12:01,137
IN FORMATION

245
00:12:01,220 --> 00:12:03,389
- Is this <i>The Mate?</i>
- This feels strange.

246
00:12:04,181 --> 00:12:06,142
Should we turn around? What should we do?

247
00:12:06,225 --> 00:12:07,643
Do you want to stand behind us?

248
00:12:07,726 --> 00:12:08,853
Yeah, let's do that.

249
00:12:08,936 --> 00:12:10,646
Then, could you go back and spread out…

250
00:12:10,729 --> 00:12:11,897
- Okay.
- Spread out?

251
00:12:12,523 --> 00:12:13,816
- All right.
- Spread out?

252
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:15,734
Do we turn around?

253
00:12:15,818 --> 00:12:16,819
Let's try it.

254
00:12:16,902 --> 00:12:18,154
Should we close our eyes?

255
00:12:18,237 --> 00:12:19,488
4-ON-4
CUPID'S ARROWS

256
00:12:20,906 --> 00:12:22,241
CHOOSE YOUR STAFF MEMBER!

257
00:12:22,324 --> 00:12:23,284
I'll go last.

258
00:12:23,367 --> 00:12:25,119
- We won't look.
- We won't.

259
00:12:26,036 --> 00:12:27,121
Let's go.

260
00:12:27,204 --> 00:12:28,873
Here we go.

261
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:31,000
You can do it all at once.

262
00:12:31,083 --> 00:12:32,835
WHO WILL THE GUESTS CHOOSE?

263
00:12:32,918 --> 00:12:33,961
Are you done?

264
00:12:34,044 --> 00:12:35,880
- Okay.
- We'll turn around now.

265
00:12:36,464 --> 00:12:37,882
One, two, three.

266
00:12:37,965 --> 00:12:40,593
AND THE RESULT?

267
00:12:41,385 --> 00:12:42,595
Almost everyone.

268
00:12:45,097 --> 00:12:46,015
Is this for real?

269
00:12:46,765 --> 00:12:48,100
I got one.

270
00:12:48,184 --> 00:12:50,352
SNEHAL CHOSE YEON-KOUNG

271
00:12:50,436 --> 00:12:52,480
One, two, three.

272
00:12:53,189 --> 00:12:57,276
NO ONE PICKED KIAN YESTERDAY

273
00:12:58,152 --> 00:13:01,238
SEUL, SANG-CHEON, AND SMITA CHOSE KIAN

274
00:13:01,322 --> 00:13:02,573
I'm so touched.

275
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,074
Thank you.

276
00:13:04,742 --> 00:13:07,119
ZUHA GOT 0 VOTES

277
00:13:07,203 --> 00:13:10,581
JUN-HO GOT 0 VOTES

278
00:13:11,332 --> 00:13:12,291
Zuha.

279
00:13:12,374 --> 00:13:13,626
Where should we start cleaning?

280
00:13:13,709 --> 00:13:15,461
- Let's work hard.
- Right.

281
00:13:15,544 --> 00:13:17,463
- Goodness.
- We're not sad at all.

282
00:13:17,546 --> 00:13:19,173
I really wanted to pick you, but…

283
00:13:19,256 --> 00:13:20,382
We're not sad at all.

284
00:13:20,466 --> 00:13:22,009
It's okay. We're not sad.

285
00:13:22,968 --> 00:13:25,721
NOT SAD WITH A STICKY ROLLER

286
00:13:25,804 --> 00:13:28,307
Jun-ho. Clean hard, okay?

287
00:13:29,183 --> 00:13:30,017
Yes, ma'am.

288
00:13:33,479 --> 00:13:37,691
NOT SAD WHILE EMPTYING A BIN

289
00:13:37,775 --> 00:13:39,527
Boss will do it outside.

290
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:40,903
So let's do it here.

291
00:13:40,986 --> 00:13:42,363
Go chat with Boss.

292
00:13:42,446 --> 00:13:43,489
YEON-KOUNG & SNEHAL

293
00:13:43,572 --> 00:13:44,657
How was it here?

294
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:46,158
It was so fun.

295
00:13:46,242 --> 00:13:49,286
I've never been this happy
throughout a stay in my life.

296
00:13:49,870 --> 00:13:50,704
Thank you.

297
00:13:50,788 --> 00:13:51,997
No, we should thank you.

298
00:13:52,081 --> 00:13:54,375
I'm so grateful you worked so hard for us.

299
00:13:54,458 --> 00:13:57,294
But you know, you two are so cheerful

300
00:13:57,378 --> 00:13:59,338
and get along so well with other people.

301
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:00,965
It made me think.

302
00:14:01,048 --> 00:14:03,384
I've spent a lot of time abroad too.

303
00:14:03,467 --> 00:14:04,927
MORE THAN 10 YEARS OVERSEAS

304
00:14:05,010 --> 00:14:10,266
So I know well how difficult it can be
to live abroad as a foreigner.

305
00:14:10,349 --> 00:14:12,643
I know how hard it can be for you.

306
00:14:12,726 --> 00:14:14,061
Please don't do that.

307
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:15,688
No, I mean it.

308
00:14:15,771 --> 00:14:18,274
Since I know how hard it can be,

309
00:14:18,357 --> 00:14:20,901
I find it very admirable.

310
00:14:22,027 --> 00:14:23,696
- Why am I suddenly crying?
- Goodness.

311
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:25,239
TEARING UP AFTER RELATING

312
00:14:25,322 --> 00:14:27,074
I'll go get some tissues.

313
00:14:27,157 --> 00:14:28,158
Why are you crying?

314
00:14:28,242 --> 00:14:29,076
I don't know.

315
00:14:29,159 --> 00:14:31,537
HUGE TOILET PAPER

316
00:14:31,620 --> 00:14:32,997
Why are you crying?

317
00:14:33,080 --> 00:14:34,373
Come here.

318
00:14:35,040 --> 00:14:35,875
Why are you crying?

319
00:14:36,667 --> 00:14:38,669
I'm young and in my twenties now,

320
00:14:38,752 --> 00:14:41,005
but I think I should live
as if I were in my thirties

321
00:14:41,088 --> 00:14:42,882
to make it easier on myself later on.

322
00:14:42,965 --> 00:14:45,217
With that in mind,
I want to enjoy my life.

323
00:14:46,010 --> 00:14:47,428
And I've always thought this.

324
00:14:47,511 --> 00:14:49,680
If I work hard for a long time,

325
00:14:49,763 --> 00:14:52,182
I can be successful in anything.

326
00:14:52,266 --> 00:14:55,311
So, I just believe and keep going,

327
00:14:55,394 --> 00:14:56,729
even if there's no path.

328
00:14:56,812 --> 00:14:59,106
Sometimes, that kind of mindset
is important.

329
00:14:59,189 --> 00:15:01,692
"Just keep going, and it'll all work out."

330
00:15:01,775 --> 00:15:04,737
It'll all build up
and pay off in the future.

331
00:15:05,613 --> 00:15:06,572
Why am I crying?

332
00:15:07,114 --> 00:15:08,490
I'm not usually like this.

333
00:15:08,574 --> 00:15:09,700
It's okay.

334
00:15:09,783 --> 00:15:11,994
- I'm sad that I'm leaving.
- I totally get it.

335
00:15:12,077 --> 00:15:13,120
It's a shame.

336
00:15:13,203 --> 00:15:14,747
Right, it is.

337
00:15:17,708 --> 00:15:18,918
- Smita?
- That's right.

338
00:15:19,001 --> 00:15:19,960
Smita, right?

339
00:15:20,044 --> 00:15:21,253
Was it okay? Did you like it?

340
00:15:21,337 --> 00:15:22,630
KIAN
CHAE-SEUL, SANG-CHEON, SMITA

341
00:15:22,713 --> 00:15:25,174
I haven't had many chances

342
00:15:25,257 --> 00:15:26,759
to get close to Korean people.

343
00:15:26,842 --> 00:15:31,305
And I got to do a lot of that here,
so I really loved that.

344
00:15:31,388 --> 00:15:32,222
I'm glad.

345
00:15:32,306 --> 00:15:33,974
I'm sad that I have to leave.

346
00:15:34,058 --> 00:15:35,059
- So…
- Honestly?

347
00:15:35,142 --> 00:15:35,976
Of course.

348
00:15:36,060 --> 00:15:37,269
Three days went by so fast.

349
00:15:37,353 --> 00:15:39,188
- Yes, it was so short.
- Tell me about it.

350
00:15:39,271 --> 00:15:42,775
On the other hand, it must be hard for you
to welcome and let people go.

351
00:15:42,858 --> 00:15:43,776
Because you get close.

352
00:15:43,859 --> 00:15:44,693
- Me?
- Yes.

353
00:15:45,277 --> 00:15:48,280
When I talk with you, Father,
it makes me feel at peace.

354
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:49,281
PEACE OF MIND

355
00:15:49,365 --> 00:15:50,199
- Seriously.
- Really?

356
00:15:50,282 --> 00:15:51,992
I don't know why I feel like that.

357
00:15:52,076 --> 00:15:53,577
- But, Kian--
- I'm put at ease.

358
00:15:53,661 --> 00:15:55,579
That's why I'm grateful
to you too, Sam-cheon.

359
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:57,623
- "Sam-cheon"?
- Thank you for coming here.

360
00:15:57,706 --> 00:15:59,667
You're such a bitch.

361
00:16:02,711 --> 00:16:03,879
"Bitch"?

362
00:16:03,963 --> 00:16:05,255
Such a bitch.

363
00:16:05,756 --> 00:16:07,049
I'm not a bitch.

364
00:16:07,132 --> 00:16:08,926
- I'm <i>bit, </i>or ray of light.
- Right, <i>bit.</i>

365
00:16:09,009 --> 00:16:10,844
- Right, <i>bit!</i>
- <i>Bit, </i>not bitch.

366
00:16:10,928 --> 00:16:12,554
IT'S MY BAD

367
00:16:13,222 --> 00:16:14,515
<i>"Bit"?</i> "Bitch"?

368
00:16:14,598 --> 00:16:15,766
Oh, "bitch"!

369
00:16:15,849 --> 00:16:16,684
HE GETS IT NOW

370
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:18,602
"You're such a bitch"!

371
00:16:21,605 --> 00:16:24,024
You were all bright like light,

372
00:16:24,108 --> 00:16:26,527
but it's off now.

373
00:16:28,028 --> 00:16:30,072
What do you mean? The light's off?

374
00:16:30,155 --> 00:16:30,990
It's off now?

375
00:16:31,073 --> 00:16:32,533
My light is off now?

376
00:16:32,616 --> 00:16:34,410
- You can feel that?
- Yes.

377
00:16:34,493 --> 00:16:36,286
- Do I look dark?
- Very dark.

378
00:16:36,870 --> 00:16:37,788
SHOCKED

379
00:16:37,871 --> 00:16:38,998
You're always stressed out.

380
00:16:39,081 --> 00:16:42,209
You know those gloomy clouds?
I can see them over you.

381
00:16:42,710 --> 00:16:46,255
A DARK BOSS

382
00:16:46,338 --> 00:16:49,258
Where did your old self go?

383
00:16:50,467 --> 00:16:53,345
I've been worried this entire time.

384
00:16:53,929 --> 00:16:57,808
First off, I planned
and built a fun house,

385
00:16:57,891 --> 00:17:00,394
but I worry someone might get hurt
because of the design.

386
00:17:00,477 --> 00:17:03,480
Well, there's nothing I can do
about that now, but it worries me.

387
00:17:04,440 --> 00:17:06,859
You came here to have fun,
but I wasn't sure

388
00:17:06,942 --> 00:17:08,402
if you found it fun here.

389
00:17:08,485 --> 00:17:10,696
I've been worried about that too.

390
00:17:10,779 --> 00:17:11,780
And safety?

391
00:17:12,322 --> 00:17:16,201
And the most important thing is
for guests to have fun here.

392
00:17:17,327 --> 00:17:18,245
It's so hard.

393
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:19,830
THAT'S WHY IT'S HARD

394
00:17:21,457 --> 00:17:22,750
<i>To tell you the truth,</i>

395
00:17:22,833 --> 00:17:24,710
I was the biggest problem.

396
00:17:25,544 --> 00:17:28,547
I was so clumsy. I felt so lost.

397
00:17:29,131 --> 00:17:30,215
Be careful there.

398
00:17:32,801 --> 00:17:34,011
<i>"Are they enjoying it?"</i>

399
00:17:34,845 --> 00:17:36,847
<i>Since I was so worried,</i>

400
00:17:36,930 --> 00:17:39,016
I couldn't have proper talks with guests.

401
00:17:39,099 --> 00:17:43,395
WHILE EVERYONE'S HAVING FUN

402
00:17:44,980 --> 00:17:46,523
Today…

403
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:54,490
KIAN WAS DEEP IN THOUGHT ALONE

404
00:17:54,573 --> 00:17:57,993
<i>I was hesitant.</i>
<i>I think I was the clumsiest one.</i>

405
00:18:04,124 --> 00:18:05,751
So when Smita said

406
00:18:05,834 --> 00:18:07,336
that I was so dark,

407
00:18:07,419 --> 00:18:10,255
I was totally stunned.

408
00:18:10,339 --> 00:18:12,007
Kian, don't worry about that.

409
00:18:13,258 --> 00:18:16,261
You must have fun
so everyone else can truly have fun.

410
00:18:16,345 --> 00:18:19,223
The solution is for you to have fun here.

411
00:18:19,848 --> 00:18:20,682
I'm sorry.

412
00:18:20,766 --> 00:18:21,642
Don't be.

413
00:18:21,725 --> 00:18:23,894
Well, I have a lot to worry about.

414
00:18:23,977 --> 00:18:25,312
I have a lot on my…

415
00:18:25,896 --> 00:18:28,899
But seriously, thank you for saying that.

416
00:18:30,109 --> 00:18:32,319
It was good advice.

417
00:18:32,402 --> 00:18:33,570
Be cheerful?

418
00:18:33,654 --> 00:18:34,863
- Yes.
- Got it.

419
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:36,573
It's really valuable advice.

420
00:18:38,534 --> 00:18:40,244
<i>It helped a lot.</i>

421
00:18:40,744 --> 00:18:42,579
I don't know if it'll work,

422
00:18:42,663 --> 00:18:45,791
but when the moment comes,
and if I approach the guests first,

423
00:18:45,874 --> 00:18:48,752
then I believe it'll be better.

424
00:18:49,878 --> 00:18:51,839
- You should go. It's 11:00 a.m.
- Right.

425
00:18:51,922 --> 00:18:54,174
- Thank you for everything, Mr. Kian.
- Thank you.

426
00:18:54,925 --> 00:18:56,343
How did the talks go?

427
00:18:56,426 --> 00:18:58,387
Smita said I was darkness.

428
00:18:58,470 --> 00:18:59,596
Darkness?

429
00:18:59,680 --> 00:19:00,806
No, not darkness.

430
00:19:00,889 --> 00:19:01,807
Darkness?

431
00:19:01,890 --> 00:19:02,808
It's not like that.

432
00:19:02,891 --> 00:19:04,852
I was so hurt.

433
00:19:05,435 --> 00:19:06,979
No, I'm joking.

434
00:19:07,062 --> 00:19:08,689
I know what you meant.

435
00:19:09,273 --> 00:19:10,816
FINALLY, WRITING IN THE VISITORS' LOG

436
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:14,611
MAY PEACE BE WITH THIS HOUSE
AND EVERYONE STAYING IN IT

437
00:19:14,695 --> 00:19:16,864
PRIEST
MIN SANG-CHEON

438
00:19:16,947 --> 00:19:19,658
THANK YOU FOR BEING SPECIAL PEOPLE
IN MY LIFE THAT I'LL REMEMBER

439
00:19:19,741 --> 00:19:20,784
SPATIAL DESIGNER
CHAE SEUL

440
00:19:21,451 --> 00:19:23,912
Wait… You two are writing a lot.

441
00:19:23,996 --> 00:19:25,873
"Kian and Kazuha,

442
00:19:25,956 --> 00:19:28,458
please don't be so stressed out."

443
00:19:30,002 --> 00:19:30,836
OLDER TWIN
SMITA

444
00:19:30,919 --> 00:19:32,546
"Jun-ho, thanks for the seaweed soup."

445
00:19:32,629 --> 00:19:34,006
That's a big heart around my name.

446
00:19:34,089 --> 00:19:35,632
I HAD SO MUCH FUN THESE THREE DAYS

447
00:19:35,716 --> 00:19:36,550
YOUNGER TWIN
SNEHAL

448
00:19:37,134 --> 00:19:38,969
- We should leave so you can…
- Yes.

449
00:19:39,052 --> 00:19:40,137
CHECKOUT TIME
11:00 A.M.

450
00:19:40,220 --> 00:19:41,180
It's been fun.

451
00:19:41,263 --> 00:19:42,431
- Thank you.
- Take care.

452
00:19:42,514 --> 00:19:43,599
We will. Thank you.

453
00:19:43,682 --> 00:19:44,725
- Be careful of snow.
- Bye!

454
00:19:47,269 --> 00:19:48,729
Good luck, Mr. Kian!

455
00:19:48,812 --> 00:19:49,938
- Okay, good luck!
- Good luck!

456
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:51,106
It's been a great time.

457
00:19:51,607 --> 00:19:53,066
I love you, Jun-ho!

458
00:19:53,150 --> 00:19:55,068
- Good luck! I love you!
- I love you!

459
00:19:55,152 --> 00:19:56,195
I love you!

460
00:19:56,278 --> 00:19:57,529
I love you all!

461
00:19:57,613 --> 00:20:00,157
SNEHAL, SMITA, SANG-CHEON, SEUL
CHECK OUT

462
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:02,201
We'll really go now.

463
00:20:06,288 --> 00:20:07,789
What? Because it's a shame to leave?

464
00:20:07,873 --> 00:20:08,707
Yes.

465
00:20:10,209 --> 00:20:13,462
<i>For young people like us</i>
<i>going through a lot of growing pains,</i>

466
00:20:13,545 --> 00:20:16,715
<i>it was where we could be innocent</i>
<i>and show our genuine smiles.</i>

467
00:20:16,798 --> 00:20:18,800
KIAN'S B&B IS "GENUINE"

468
00:20:19,384 --> 00:20:21,803
<i>It reminded me of when we'd play</i>
<i>hide-and-seek as kids.</i>

469
00:20:21,887 --> 00:20:22,930
<i>That innocence.</i>

470
00:20:23,013 --> 00:20:24,431
KIAN'S B&B IS "INNOCENCE"

471
00:20:24,514 --> 00:20:27,809
If I think about everything
I experienced in this house,

472
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:29,770
<i>despite being foreigners,</i>
<i>we were like family.</i>

473
00:20:29,853 --> 00:20:30,812
KIAN'S B&B IS "FAMILY"

474
00:20:30,896 --> 00:20:33,148
<i>So I was so grateful.</i>

475
00:20:33,232 --> 00:20:37,236
<i>There's no guesthouse host</i>
<i>who treats their guests this well.</i>

476
00:20:38,070 --> 00:20:39,363
I'm sure of it.

477
00:20:40,822 --> 00:20:43,242
- Bye. I had a great time.
- Bye, Kian's B&B.

478
00:20:43,325 --> 00:20:46,036
- Seriously, it'll be fond memories.
- I had so much fun.

479
00:20:46,119 --> 00:20:48,580
- It was like a dream, wasn't it?
- It was.

480
00:20:48,664 --> 00:20:50,832
- It really was.
- We made the best memories ever!

481
00:20:51,875 --> 00:20:53,043
We're going home now.

482
00:20:53,126 --> 00:20:55,963
KIAN'S B&B

483
00:20:57,881 --> 00:20:59,258
- Again, it's…
- Yeah.

484
00:20:59,341 --> 00:21:00,634
- Again.
- They're all gone.

485
00:21:00,717 --> 00:21:03,053
- Goodness.
- This very feeling.

486
00:21:03,136 --> 00:21:05,013
- So empty.
- This feeling after they leave.

487
00:21:05,097 --> 00:21:06,556
Another four have gone.

488
00:21:10,644 --> 00:21:11,895
Is all the cleaning finished?

489
00:21:11,979 --> 00:21:12,813
Yes, it is.

490
00:21:12,896 --> 00:21:15,399
I was exempt from cleaning today.

491
00:21:15,899 --> 00:21:17,067
That's a good thing.

492
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:18,902
- By the way, Jun-ho.
- Yes?

493
00:21:18,986 --> 00:21:21,530
They announced the news yesterday
about us joining the show.

494
00:21:21,613 --> 00:21:22,489
Right.

495
00:21:22,572 --> 00:21:23,657
You're pretty popular.

496
00:21:23,740 --> 00:21:25,409
- Me?
- He's very popular.

497
00:21:25,492 --> 00:21:27,035
- No way.
- I was so surprised.

498
00:21:27,119 --> 00:21:28,370
No, I'm not.

499
00:21:28,996 --> 00:21:31,164
- Gosh, Jun-ho's so popular.
- No, not at all.

500
00:21:31,665 --> 00:21:32,874
So are you all right?

501
00:21:32,958 --> 00:21:33,875
- Me?
- Yeah.

502
00:21:33,959 --> 00:21:36,086
You're so popular on social media,

503
00:21:36,169 --> 00:21:38,088
but not so much here.

504
00:21:39,006 --> 00:21:42,092
JUN-HO HAS RECEIVED A TOTAL 0 VOTES SO FAR

505
00:21:42,175 --> 00:21:44,261
You're in the kitchen all the time.

506
00:21:44,344 --> 00:21:47,055
- I work so hard to clean up there.
- Right.

507
00:21:47,139 --> 00:21:48,640
Why do you think it's cleaner now?

508
00:21:48,724 --> 00:21:49,933
CLEAN KITCHEN THANKS TO JUN-HO

509
00:21:50,017 --> 00:21:51,685
So you believe

510
00:21:51,768 --> 00:21:53,020
you got

511
00:21:53,103 --> 00:21:54,313
zero votes…

512
00:21:54,396 --> 00:21:56,398
- Because…
- Because all you've done is work?

513
00:21:56,481 --> 00:21:57,941
- Right.
- "All you've done."

514
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:59,609
That's what I believe.

515
00:22:00,360 --> 00:22:02,988
But I don't dwell on that.

516
00:22:03,488 --> 00:22:05,115
- He makes that sounds cool.
- Yeah.

517
00:22:05,198 --> 00:22:06,908
I'll keep working hard

518
00:22:06,992 --> 00:22:09,911
so you can take good care of our guests.

519
00:22:09,995 --> 00:22:11,747
I'll do my best to support you.

520
00:22:11,830 --> 00:22:12,664
VERY DETERMINED

521
00:22:12,748 --> 00:22:13,957
- What?
- He's the best.

522
00:22:14,041 --> 00:22:15,876
12:00 P.M.

523
00:22:15,959 --> 00:22:17,669
Don't you feel hungry?

524
00:22:17,753 --> 00:22:18,712
Should we eat out?

525
00:22:18,795 --> 00:22:19,629
I'd like that.

526
00:22:21,173 --> 00:22:22,924
- I want to eat at a restaurant.
- Yes.

527
00:22:23,008 --> 00:22:24,217
Chinese food.

528
00:22:24,301 --> 00:22:26,428
Then, shall we have Chinese food
and talk a little?

529
00:22:26,511 --> 00:22:27,637
Should we go now?

530
00:22:27,721 --> 00:22:29,181
Let's go. I'm hungry.

531
00:22:29,264 --> 00:22:30,098
Okay.

532
00:22:31,224 --> 00:22:32,100
You look cool.

533
00:22:32,184 --> 00:22:33,185
- What?
- You look cool.

534
00:22:33,268 --> 00:22:34,102
- Really?
- Yes.

535
00:22:36,146 --> 00:22:38,190
You look a bit like a delinquent.

536
00:22:38,690 --> 00:22:39,775
- If I make this face?
- Yes?

537
00:22:39,858 --> 00:22:41,234
Yes, with that expression.

538
00:22:41,318 --> 00:22:42,360
- Feeling comfortable?
- Yes.

539
00:22:42,444 --> 00:22:43,779
Good. Me too.

540
00:22:44,404 --> 00:22:45,238
I'm scared.

541
00:22:47,365 --> 00:22:48,992
ZUHA FEELS VERY COMFORTABLE NOW

542
00:22:49,076 --> 00:22:51,912
- By the way, Boss is so lucky.
- Why?

543
00:22:51,995 --> 00:22:55,791
These two are doing Kian's B&B
as their first variety show.

544
00:22:55,874 --> 00:22:57,042
I'm so grateful.

545
00:22:58,043 --> 00:22:59,419
You're so blessed.

546
00:23:00,796 --> 00:23:02,380
Isn't meeting you the biggest blessing?

547
00:23:02,464 --> 00:23:04,132
What's gotten into you all of a sudden?

548
00:23:04,216 --> 00:23:05,759
Why are you being like that to me?

549
00:23:05,842 --> 00:23:08,053
I think what he heard keeps bothering him.

550
00:23:08,136 --> 00:23:08,970
Very dark.

551
00:23:09,054 --> 00:23:10,263
Right?

552
00:23:10,347 --> 00:23:12,766
Whenever I made eye contact, I felt bad.

553
00:23:13,517 --> 00:23:16,186
We don't know which one is the real you.

554
00:23:16,269 --> 00:23:18,355
The me from today
and yesterday are both real.

555
00:23:19,481 --> 00:23:20,607
I've become so cautious.

556
00:23:20,690 --> 00:23:21,733
This is the place.

557
00:23:22,234 --> 00:23:23,068
Hello.

558
00:23:28,907 --> 00:23:30,033
YEON-KOUNG SETS THE TABLE

559
00:23:30,117 --> 00:23:31,868
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

560
00:23:33,078 --> 00:23:35,664
Yeon-koung's so good at being in a group.

561
00:23:36,998 --> 00:23:39,417
I think you're a master
of group activities.

562
00:23:39,501 --> 00:23:40,710
What did I do?

563
00:23:40,794 --> 00:23:42,879
I mean, it seems like
you were made to be in a group.

564
00:23:42,963 --> 00:23:44,631
It's because I've been in groups a lot.

565
00:23:44,714 --> 00:23:47,467
But you two have also spent
a lot of time in groups,

566
00:23:47,551 --> 00:23:48,844
so you must be used to it too.

567
00:23:48,927 --> 00:23:50,846
- You still live with the other members.
- Right.

568
00:23:50,929 --> 00:23:52,848
LE SSERAFIM members still live together?

569
00:23:52,931 --> 00:23:53,765
Yes.

570
00:23:53,849 --> 00:23:56,309
- A group of two and a group of three.
- Really?

571
00:23:56,393 --> 00:23:59,771
When you quit ballet to become a singer,
what was the hardest part?

572
00:23:59,855 --> 00:24:02,774
- I wasn't good at Korean at first.
- The language?

573
00:24:02,858 --> 00:24:05,152
So it took a while
to get close to the other members.

574
00:24:05,235 --> 00:24:06,069
Right.

575
00:24:06,153 --> 00:24:07,863
But your pronunciation's so good.

576
00:24:07,946 --> 00:24:09,739
- It's like a native speaker.
- It's great.

577
00:24:09,823 --> 00:24:12,200
- Really?
- People wouldn't know you're Japanese.

578
00:24:12,284 --> 00:24:13,743
- You really think so?
- Yeah.

579
00:24:14,286 --> 00:24:16,830
Did you go somewhere
and learn how to give compliments?

580
00:24:18,165 --> 00:24:19,207
"Let's praise each other."

581
00:24:19,291 --> 00:24:21,626
It feels like "Our Boss Has Changed."

582
00:24:21,710 --> 00:24:23,211
- It's here.
- Pardon me.

583
00:24:24,045 --> 00:24:25,964
- It looks so good.
- The portions are huge.

584
00:24:27,132 --> 00:24:28,258
Isn't it so good?

585
00:24:30,093 --> 00:24:31,386
There's a lot of seafood.

586
00:24:52,115 --> 00:24:55,410
I think we're eating much more today
than we have so far.

587
00:24:55,493 --> 00:24:58,330
Because we've been working hard.

588
00:25:00,081 --> 00:25:01,124
Made with flour…

589
00:25:01,208 --> 00:25:03,043
Should I make pizza today?

590
00:25:03,126 --> 00:25:03,960
It's doable.

591
00:25:04,044 --> 00:25:05,003
BOSS IS TODAY'S CHEF

592
00:25:05,086 --> 00:25:07,339
- How?
- Are you going to make the dough?

593
00:25:08,006 --> 00:25:09,633
I can make it in a frying pan.

594
00:25:10,675 --> 00:25:12,969
When I was a kid,
that's how I always did it.

595
00:25:13,053 --> 00:25:14,095
It sounds good.

596
00:25:14,596 --> 00:25:16,640
It's not cliché,
but I've also never heard of it.

597
00:25:17,224 --> 00:25:18,558
Like kimchi pizza.

598
00:25:18,642 --> 00:25:20,685
Kimchi cheese pizza.

599
00:25:20,769 --> 00:25:22,187
Right, kimchi cheese pizza.

600
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:24,272
- Cheese sounds good.
- That sounds delicious.

601
00:25:24,356 --> 00:25:25,523
Cheese is a must.

602
00:25:25,607 --> 00:25:26,566
Thank you for the food.

603
00:25:26,650 --> 00:25:28,193
- Thank you.
- Thank you.

604
00:25:28,276 --> 00:25:30,695
AFTER BUYING PIZZA INGREDIENTS
AT THE MARKET

605
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:31,696
How about some coffee?

606
00:25:31,780 --> 00:25:33,448
THEY WILL BUY COFFEE TO GO

607
00:25:33,531 --> 00:25:35,200
That was really fun last night.

608
00:25:35,283 --> 00:25:36,785
- What?
- The photo game.

609
00:25:36,868 --> 00:25:38,411
- It was better than I thought.
- It was.

610
00:25:38,495 --> 00:25:39,454
STARING

611
00:25:39,537 --> 00:25:40,956
- It was fun.
- Right?

612
00:25:41,039 --> 00:25:42,457
Did you tint the lenses?

613
00:25:42,540 --> 00:25:44,292
- Yes.
- Why did you do that?

614
00:25:44,376 --> 00:25:47,337
It kind of makes me look
like a fashionista.

615
00:25:47,420 --> 00:25:48,505
To look stylish?

616
00:25:48,588 --> 00:25:50,131
Don't I look stylish?

617
00:25:50,882 --> 00:25:53,051
I thought it was for your eyesight.

618
00:25:54,094 --> 00:25:55,804
What would you know about fashion?

619
00:25:55,887 --> 00:25:57,347
I know a thing or two.

620
00:25:57,973 --> 00:25:59,599
We should ask Kazuha.

621
00:25:59,683 --> 00:26:00,767
- GV?
- GV.

622
00:26:00,850 --> 00:26:01,768
- GV.
- Very trendy.

623
00:26:01,851 --> 00:26:03,019
GV.

624
00:26:03,103 --> 00:26:04,312
- GV?
- GV.

625
00:26:04,396 --> 00:26:05,647
You don't know, do you?

626
00:26:05,730 --> 00:26:07,148
- GF?
- GV.

627
00:26:07,232 --> 00:26:08,858
Try to guess the meaning.

628
00:26:08,942 --> 00:26:10,151
It's "GV," not "GF."

629
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:11,444
Like "get fucked"?

630
00:26:11,528 --> 00:26:12,737
That's a curse word.

631
00:26:12,821 --> 00:26:14,906
It doesn't stand for "fuck."

632
00:26:14,990 --> 00:26:16,366
So what does that mean?

633
00:26:16,449 --> 00:26:17,367
- Tell him again.
- What?

634
00:26:17,450 --> 00:26:18,910
Pronounce it accurately.

635
00:26:19,869 --> 00:26:20,704
GV.

636
00:26:20,787 --> 00:26:21,621
DV?

637
00:26:21,705 --> 00:26:22,956
GV.

638
00:26:23,039 --> 00:26:23,873
DV?

639
00:26:23,957 --> 00:26:24,874
No, it's…

640
00:26:25,500 --> 00:26:27,377
You're cursing at me, aren't you?

641
00:26:27,460 --> 00:26:28,628
- G.
- G.

642
00:26:28,712 --> 00:26:29,796
GV.

643
00:26:29,879 --> 00:26:31,006
GV?

644
00:26:31,673 --> 00:26:34,175
GB?

645
00:26:34,259 --> 00:26:35,093
Is it Japanese?

646
00:26:35,176 --> 00:26:36,011
Of course not.

647
00:26:36,094 --> 00:26:37,637
- Your coffee is ready.
- Thank you.

648
00:26:37,721 --> 00:26:38,847
What does it mean?

649
00:26:39,347 --> 00:26:41,433
- "Good vibes."
- "Good vibes."

650
00:26:41,516 --> 00:26:42,517
It stands for that?

651
00:26:42,600 --> 00:26:44,144
- That's the new slang these days.
- Yes.

652
00:26:44,227 --> 00:26:45,729
Did you know what it meant?

653
00:26:45,812 --> 00:26:47,480
- Come on.
- Of course, she knew.

654
00:26:47,564 --> 00:26:48,481
Boss.

655
00:26:48,565 --> 00:26:49,399
You really knew?

656
00:26:49,482 --> 00:26:50,567
Of course, I knew.

657
00:26:50,650 --> 00:26:51,776
Gosh, it's GB.

658
00:26:53,111 --> 00:26:54,612
I told you it's not "GB."

659
00:26:55,405 --> 00:26:56,239
What?

660
00:26:56,323 --> 00:26:57,615
The scenery's pretty GB.

661
00:26:57,699 --> 00:26:58,783
"GV."

662
00:26:58,867 --> 00:26:59,951
- It's GV.
- V.

663
00:27:00,035 --> 00:27:00,869
It means "good."

664
00:27:00,952 --> 00:27:02,203
- Right, good.
- Yeah.

665
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:04,497
It really has GV.

666
00:27:06,082 --> 00:27:07,834
The clouds make it look so cool.

667
00:27:07,917 --> 00:27:08,752
Right.

668
00:27:08,835 --> 00:27:10,670
It totally has GV.

669
00:27:10,754 --> 00:27:12,005
CAH.

670
00:27:12,088 --> 00:27:14,049
- You're talking about me, aren't you?
- CAH.

671
00:27:14,132 --> 00:27:15,675
- "Clueless as hell."
- What?

672
00:27:15,759 --> 00:27:17,135
Boss is CAH.

673
00:27:22,432 --> 00:27:23,558
SURFING IN YANGYANG

674
00:27:25,101 --> 00:27:27,896
- Is this the popular county of Yangyang?
- The weather's so nice.

675
00:27:27,979 --> 00:27:29,689
So this is the coastal road.

676
00:27:29,773 --> 00:27:31,483
This is a hot spot for surfers.

677
00:27:31,566 --> 00:27:33,943
Winter surfing. Look at the waves.

678
00:27:38,615 --> 00:27:39,991
This is so nice.

679
00:27:40,075 --> 00:27:40,992
Let's go.

680
00:27:41,076 --> 00:27:42,160
JUKDO BEACH

681
00:27:42,243 --> 00:27:43,286
<i>The waves are nice.</i>

682
00:27:43,370 --> 00:27:45,163
AFTER ENJOYING A WINTER BEACH

683
00:27:45,747 --> 00:27:48,124
THEY TRY SURFING

684
00:27:49,334 --> 00:27:51,044
WOBBLING

685
00:27:52,921 --> 00:27:55,256
WOBBLING HERE TOO

686
00:28:10,814 --> 00:28:12,690
I still have a salty taste in my mouth.

687
00:28:12,774 --> 00:28:14,359
My hands are shaking.

688
00:28:15,110 --> 00:28:16,069
The ski resort.

689
00:28:16,152 --> 00:28:17,320
We should go now.

690
00:28:18,405 --> 00:28:19,781
GI-PYO, JIN-AN, YOUNG-HYUN, JUN-HO

691
00:28:19,864 --> 00:28:20,698
YONGPYONG SKI RESORT

692
00:28:20,782 --> 00:28:22,033
<i>It's my first time this year.</i>

693
00:28:22,117 --> 00:28:23,618
<i>I haven't ridden in ages.</i>

694
00:28:27,414 --> 00:28:28,790
<i>I'm nervous.</i>

695
00:28:29,290 --> 00:28:30,792
I want to race.

696
00:28:37,006 --> 00:28:38,216
That's a nice speed.

697
00:28:39,717 --> 00:28:41,136
Gi-pyo's skiing well.

698
00:28:43,221 --> 00:28:44,139
This feels good.

699
00:28:50,687 --> 00:28:51,938
The view today is so…

700
00:28:52,021 --> 00:28:54,149
I can't believe how it changes every day.

701
00:28:54,733 --> 00:28:56,276
It's snowing like rain.

702
00:28:56,359 --> 00:28:57,861
MORNING AT THE SNOWY KIAN'S B&B

703
00:28:58,486 --> 00:29:00,071
It's sleeting.

704
00:29:00,155 --> 00:29:01,448
SLEETING IN THE AFTERNOON

705
00:29:02,240 --> 00:29:03,199
I'll carry it.

706
00:29:03,283 --> 00:29:04,868
GROCERIES

707
00:29:04,951 --> 00:29:06,619
- Thanks.
- You drove.

708
00:29:07,454 --> 00:29:09,831
Thank you. You're the symbol
of being thoughtful.

709
00:29:10,457 --> 00:29:11,458
Very thoughtful.

710
00:29:11,541 --> 00:29:13,585
- The epitome.
- Our boss has changed.

711
00:29:13,668 --> 00:29:14,836
Want me to carry this too?

712
00:29:14,919 --> 00:29:16,004
Hey, come on.

713
00:29:17,005 --> 00:29:19,215
It feels like we're the ones
returning from a trip.

714
00:29:19,716 --> 00:29:20,592
- Right.
- Right.

715
00:29:20,675 --> 00:29:22,677
These little trips help you recharge.

716
00:29:22,761 --> 00:29:23,803
- I think it's nice.
- It is.

717
00:29:23,887 --> 00:29:24,929
RETURNING AFTER RECHARGING

718
00:29:25,597 --> 00:29:26,431
1:30 P.M.

719
00:29:26,514 --> 00:29:27,891
We should…

720
00:29:27,974 --> 00:29:29,058
Move it up?

721
00:29:29,142 --> 00:29:29,976
Can you do it?

722
00:29:30,059 --> 00:29:31,060
MOVING IT TO THE KITCHEN

723
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:33,563
Wait, I'll do it.
Hold on. I'll go up first.

724
00:29:35,315 --> 00:29:36,232
ZUHA FROM DOWNSTAIRS

725
00:29:36,316 --> 00:29:37,150
Lift it up.

726
00:29:37,233 --> 00:29:38,234
Hold on.

727
00:29:38,735 --> 00:29:39,569
Lift.

728
00:29:40,195 --> 00:29:41,780
PUTTING IT ON HER HEAD

729
00:29:45,325 --> 00:29:46,159
Hey, you're strong!

730
00:29:49,037 --> 00:29:50,371
- Be careful.
- Does it reach?

731
00:29:50,455 --> 00:29:51,372
VERY CLOSE

732
00:29:51,456 --> 00:29:52,624
Just a bit higher.

733
00:29:52,707 --> 00:29:53,792
ONE MORE PUSH

734
00:29:55,460 --> 00:29:57,378
- Way to go!
- Don't drop it.

735
00:29:57,879 --> 00:29:58,963
If you do, I'll die.

736
00:29:59,047 --> 00:30:00,799
THEY DID IT THANKS TO STRONG ZUHA

737
00:30:02,509 --> 00:30:03,676
Is your head okay?

738
00:30:05,428 --> 00:30:07,222
It's fine. But it's a mess.

739
00:30:07,305 --> 00:30:08,348
SIDE EFFECT OF STRONG ZUHA

740
00:30:08,431 --> 00:30:09,265
It's ruined.

741
00:30:09,349 --> 00:30:10,809
We just need to do laundry.

742
00:30:10,892 --> 00:30:12,018
- Laundry?
- Yes.

743
00:30:13,311 --> 00:30:15,063
If we stomp on them, it won't take long.

744
00:30:15,146 --> 00:30:16,105
4 DAYS WORTH OF LAUNDRY

745
00:30:16,189 --> 00:30:17,232
TOWELS & SAUNA CLOTHES

746
00:30:17,315 --> 00:30:18,483
IN THE SAUNA LAST NIGHT

747
00:30:18,566 --> 00:30:20,527
Should we just use
the jacuzzi to do laundry?

748
00:30:21,694 --> 00:30:23,112
Should we just do it there?

749
00:30:24,239 --> 00:30:26,199
I think it's a good idea. Let's do that.

750
00:30:26,282 --> 00:30:27,617
JACUZZI IS THE LAUNDRY SPOT

751
00:30:27,700 --> 00:30:29,702
But we have to hang them afterwards.

752
00:30:29,786 --> 00:30:30,620
In there?

753
00:30:30,703 --> 00:30:33,164
Dry them in the sauna
and hang some outside.

754
00:30:33,248 --> 00:30:34,249
SAUNA IS THE DRYING ROOM

755
00:30:34,332 --> 00:30:35,291
I'll give it a try.

756
00:30:35,375 --> 00:30:37,210
All right, let's do it together. Okay.

757
00:30:38,920 --> 00:30:39,963
- Laundry?
- Yes.

758
00:30:40,046 --> 00:30:41,589
BOSS IS PLANNING A MURAL

759
00:30:41,673 --> 00:30:42,966
- Sorry?
- Where do we do laundry?

760
00:30:43,049 --> 00:30:43,883
- Upstairs.
- Upstairs?

761
00:30:44,467 --> 00:30:45,468
How do we move it up?

762
00:30:45,552 --> 00:30:47,095
- Up there…
- Yes?

763
00:30:47,178 --> 00:30:50,348
There's a basket the guests used
to bring the food down yesterday.

764
00:30:50,431 --> 00:30:51,266
This one?

765
00:30:51,975 --> 00:30:53,977
Let's use that to move these one by one.

766
00:30:56,020 --> 00:30:57,856
They must've sweat a lot last night.

767
00:30:57,939 --> 00:30:58,773
4 DAYS OF LAUNDRY

768
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:00,859
I sweat a lot last night.

769
00:31:00,942 --> 00:31:02,861
Right? They're all so wet.

770
00:31:02,944 --> 00:31:03,987
WET

771
00:31:04,070 --> 00:31:05,488
- Zuha, try pulling it up.
- Okay.

772
00:31:05,572 --> 00:31:06,906
This should be doable.

773
00:31:07,699 --> 00:31:09,325
- It's light still enough, right?
- Yes.

774
00:31:09,409 --> 00:31:11,077
Empty it and bring it back down.

775
00:31:20,920 --> 00:31:23,047
Geez, it stinks.

776
00:31:23,631 --> 00:31:24,883
LET'S GO, STRONG ZUHA

777
00:31:25,925 --> 00:31:26,926
You're pretty strong.

778
00:31:27,010 --> 00:31:28,094
EASILY PULLS UP SECOND LOAD

779
00:31:28,177 --> 00:31:30,930
THIRD LOAD FOLLOWS IMMEDIATELY

780
00:31:34,475 --> 00:31:35,518
You're good at this.

781
00:31:36,060 --> 00:31:37,520
LAUNDRY BOX IS EMPTY NOW

782
00:31:37,604 --> 00:31:39,355
Okay. The last one.

783
00:31:40,106 --> 00:31:40,982
Unbelievable, Zuha.

784
00:31:41,065 --> 00:31:42,233
PULLS UP BASKET A LAST TIME

785
00:31:42,317 --> 00:31:43,234
Okay.

786
00:31:43,318 --> 00:31:44,360
THE PILE IS AS BIG AS ZUHA

787
00:31:44,444 --> 00:31:47,113
Everyone, it's all upstairs now.

788
00:31:48,156 --> 00:31:49,115
I got a call.

789
00:31:50,158 --> 00:31:51,242
The phone's ringing.

790
00:31:53,578 --> 00:31:54,579
Hello?

791
00:31:54,662 --> 00:31:57,582
<i>Hello?</i>

792
00:31:59,667 --> 00:32:00,752
What?

