00:41:51,133 --> 00:41:52,927
How low are you going to go?

1055
00:41:55,012 --> 00:41:57,306
Yeon-koung, could you help me
wring this out too?

1056
00:41:57,389 --> 00:41:58,516
It's my shirt.

1057
00:41:59,099 --> 00:42:00,935
Please help me wring out my shirt.

1058
00:42:01,018 --> 00:42:01,852
My shirt…

1059
00:42:02,520 --> 00:42:03,562
Thank you.

1060
00:42:06,357 --> 00:42:09,360
Yeon-koung, while we're at it,
could you wring out my pants too?

1061
00:42:09,443 --> 00:42:11,570
Damn it. For crying out loud.

1062
00:42:12,905 --> 00:42:13,906
These too…

1063
00:42:18,786 --> 00:42:22,039
I don't think the sauna
has enough space for all these.

1064
00:42:22,122 --> 00:42:22,957
You're right.

1065
00:42:23,541 --> 00:42:24,667
I'll go start hanging them.

1066
00:42:24,750 --> 00:42:26,210
DRYING IN THE SAUNA

1067
00:42:27,002 --> 00:42:29,838
SAUNA DRYING ROOM IS OPEN

1068
00:42:31,340 --> 00:42:32,967
Goodness. Geez.

1069
00:42:35,636 --> 00:42:38,389
SUDDENLY ATTACKED

1070
00:42:38,973 --> 00:42:42,643
JUST A MOMENT AGO ON THE 2ND FLOOR

1071
00:42:45,354 --> 00:42:46,188
Good job.

1072
00:42:46,897 --> 00:42:47,856
Don't your wrists hurt?

1073
00:42:47,940 --> 00:42:49,024
YEON-KOUNG'S NO-LOOK THROW

1074
00:42:49,108 --> 00:42:50,818
- Goodness. Geez.
- Goodness, Boss.

1075
00:42:50,901 --> 00:42:52,278
SHE THREW IT WHEN HE WAS GONE

1076
00:42:52,361 --> 00:42:54,530
HE SUDDENLY APPEARS

1077
00:42:55,281 --> 00:42:56,532
SURPRISED

1078
00:42:56,615 --> 00:42:58,284
You did that on purpose, didn't you?

1079
00:42:58,784 --> 00:43:00,828
No way. I'm so sorry, Boss.

1080
00:43:01,412 --> 00:43:03,414
Since she played volleyball,
she hit me directly.

1081
00:43:03,497 --> 00:43:04,665
I'm sorry, Boss.

1082
00:43:06,083 --> 00:43:09,253
IT FEELS GOOD FOR SOME REASON

1083
00:43:10,129 --> 00:43:15,009
SHE TRIES TO TIME IT AGAIN

1084
00:43:17,052 --> 00:43:17,886
Geez.

1085
00:43:18,929 --> 00:43:20,389
It's so dangerous here.

1086
00:43:27,354 --> 00:43:28,606
Geez, there's no more space.

1087
00:43:28,689 --> 00:43:29,523
- No more?
- What?

1088
00:43:29,607 --> 00:43:31,191
NOT ENOUGH SPACE TO DRY THEM

1089
00:43:31,275 --> 00:43:32,109
This is bad.

1090
00:43:32,192 --> 00:43:33,027
STILL MORE TO DRY

1091
00:43:33,110 --> 00:43:34,987
Maybe we can use some ropes…

1092
00:43:35,904 --> 00:43:38,616
Right, we have these ropes.
They're perfect.

1093
00:43:39,116 --> 00:43:40,701
Yeon-koung, can't we use these?

1094
00:43:40,784 --> 00:43:41,744
MAKING A CLOTHESLINE

1095
00:43:41,827 --> 00:43:43,412
If we tie these up in there…

1096
00:43:44,163 --> 00:43:47,916
If we put them here, will they hold?

1097
00:43:48,417 --> 00:43:49,251
Tie it here and…

1098
00:43:49,335 --> 00:43:50,961
And tie it somewhere over there.

1099
00:43:51,045 --> 00:43:52,546
What about the door handle?

1100
00:43:52,630 --> 00:43:54,465
Then, if we tie it here…

1101
00:43:55,799 --> 00:43:56,925
That would make three lines.

1102
00:43:57,009 --> 00:43:57,968
It's not bad.

1103
00:43:58,052 --> 00:43:59,261
EXTRA SPACE SECURED WITH ROPES

1104
00:43:59,345 --> 00:44:00,471
Good idea.

1105
00:44:01,639 --> 00:44:03,265
- They'll dry really well.
- Right.

1106
00:44:05,351 --> 00:44:06,352
Jun-ho.

1107
00:44:07,311 --> 00:44:08,562
Look at how much space

1108
00:44:08,646 --> 00:44:10,147
his clothes are taking up.

1109
00:44:12,650 --> 00:44:15,694
BOSS'S PAIR OF PANTS 1,
PAIR OF PANTS 2, SWEATSHIRT

1110
00:44:15,778 --> 00:44:18,989
That's right. Laundry includes
all of our clothes, you know.

1111
00:44:21,992 --> 00:44:23,744
Stop looking at my clothes.

1112
00:44:23,827 --> 00:44:24,662
How many are there?

1113
00:44:24,745 --> 00:44:26,914
- Look at something else.
- How many are there?

1114
00:44:27,414 --> 00:44:29,541
I wanted to wash my clothes
while I was here.

1115
00:44:29,625 --> 00:44:31,293
FOR THE REMAINING LAUNDRY

1116
00:44:31,377 --> 00:44:32,252
A long line?

1117
00:44:32,753 --> 00:44:33,796
We can just tie it there.

1118
00:44:33,879 --> 00:44:34,713
ONE END ON THE TOP

1119
00:44:34,797 --> 00:44:35,631
Okay.

1120
00:44:36,298 --> 00:44:38,008
We should tie it up here.

1121
00:44:38,092 --> 00:44:39,218
OTHER END BEHIND THE DISHRAG

1122
00:44:39,843 --> 00:44:40,719
Hey, this is…

1123
00:44:45,182 --> 00:44:46,016
Okay.

1124
00:44:46,100 --> 00:44:48,185
- Let's hang the rest on this.
- It's high.

1125
00:44:48,268 --> 00:44:49,103
Nice.

1126
00:44:53,732 --> 00:44:55,651
I feel bad now
about having my clothes washed.

1127
00:44:57,903 --> 00:45:00,614
Add your clothes to the box
if you have any.

1128
00:45:01,198 --> 00:45:03,075
I'll wash them at home
with my washing machine.

1129
00:45:03,158 --> 00:45:04,535
No, I'll wash them for you.

1130
00:45:07,496 --> 00:45:09,164
Now, it really feels like Kian's B&B.

1131
00:45:09,248 --> 00:45:10,499
THE BIZARRE LAUNDRY'S DONE

1132
00:45:12,042 --> 00:45:13,627
EXHAUSTED

1133
00:45:13,710 --> 00:45:14,545
Hey!

1134
00:45:15,295 --> 00:45:16,171
- I'm hungry.
- Me too.

1135
00:45:16,255 --> 00:45:17,714
- It's all been digested.
- Right?

1136
00:45:17,798 --> 00:45:18,966
Get some rest.

1137
00:45:19,049 --> 00:45:19,883
- Yeah.
- I'll cook.

1138
00:45:19,967 --> 00:45:21,677
- Rest up and call me later.
- Okay.

1139
00:45:21,760 --> 00:45:23,345
- Call us if you need us.
- Okay.

1140
00:45:23,429 --> 00:45:27,015
KIAN GOES TO COOK DINNER RIGHT AWAY

1141
00:45:27,641 --> 00:45:28,642
Geez.

1142
00:45:28,725 --> 00:45:33,355
HE WASHES THE CUTTING BOARD
HE USED TO CUT THE SOAP

1143
00:45:33,939 --> 00:45:35,357
"Making a pizza in a frying pan."

1144
00:45:40,154 --> 00:45:41,405
Hello?

1145
00:45:41,488 --> 00:45:43,323
<i>Hello, we're supposed to check in today.</i>

1146
00:45:43,407 --> 00:45:44,241
A NEW GUEST CALLS

1147
00:45:44,324 --> 00:45:45,284
Yes, hello.

1148
00:45:45,367 --> 00:45:48,328
<i>- Where should we go and by what time?</i>
- What?

1149
00:45:48,412 --> 00:45:51,915
By 4:00 p.m., you can come
to the address I'll send you.

1150
00:45:51,999 --> 00:45:53,000
<i>Okay.</i>

1151
00:45:53,083 --> 00:45:55,419
<i>- Address? Okay.</i>
- How many of you are there?

1152
00:45:55,502 --> 00:45:56,670
<i>There are two of us.</i>

1153
00:45:56,753 --> 00:45:57,963
- Two people?
<i>- Yes.</i>

1154
00:45:58,046 --> 00:45:59,131
All right.

1155
00:45:59,214 --> 00:46:00,924
<i>- Thank you.</i>
- Bye.

1156
00:46:01,008 --> 00:46:01,967
<i>Thank you.</i>

1157
00:46:03,469 --> 00:46:05,179
Did you hear that? Two more are coming.

1158
00:46:05,262 --> 00:46:06,555
At 4:00 p.m., right?

1159
00:46:06,638 --> 00:46:07,473
3:25 A.M.

1160
00:46:07,556 --> 00:46:08,682
That's pretty soon.

1161
00:46:08,765 --> 00:46:10,726
Then, I should make two more servings.

1162
00:46:10,809 --> 00:46:11,977
12 GUESTS IN TOTAL

1163
00:46:12,060 --> 00:46:14,813
We should give them welcome drinks later.

1164
00:46:14,897 --> 00:46:16,398
Right. Should I make them?

1165
00:46:16,482 --> 00:46:20,319
Yesterday, we just mixed
lemon juice with water, but…

1166
00:46:22,237 --> 00:46:24,114
They didn't finish them.

1167
00:46:24,198 --> 00:46:25,240
I should clean up.

1168
00:46:25,324 --> 00:46:27,576
FOUND THE FINISHED THE WELCOME DRINKS

1169
00:46:28,744 --> 00:46:30,496
- This.
- How much did you add?

1170
00:46:30,579 --> 00:46:33,290
I don't remember how much,
but it was a lot.

1171
00:46:33,373 --> 00:46:35,542
But they said it was a bit too sour.

1172
00:46:35,626 --> 00:46:36,585
A LOT LIKE YESTERDAY

1173
00:46:36,668 --> 00:46:37,794
They couldn't drink it.

1174
00:46:39,296 --> 00:46:40,130
How is it?

1175
00:46:41,632 --> 00:46:42,883
- This is crazy.
- Really?

1176
00:46:45,093 --> 00:46:46,762
TINGLING

1177
00:46:47,346 --> 00:46:49,723
I think this might actually kill you.

1178
00:46:50,516 --> 00:46:51,391
I'm sweating.

1179
00:46:51,475 --> 00:46:55,312
I guess we did make them undrinkable.

1180
00:46:55,395 --> 00:46:57,272
What should we add to make them delicious?

1181
00:46:57,356 --> 00:46:59,191
- The golden ratio…
- Do we have any honey?

1182
00:46:59,274 --> 00:47:00,150
Honey?

1183
00:47:00,234 --> 00:47:02,402
Boss, is there honey up there?

1184
00:47:02,486 --> 00:47:06,323
Honey? There's <i>oligodang.</i>
But I don't see honey. You want it?

1185
00:47:06,406 --> 00:47:07,574
- Yes.
- Here.

1186
00:47:07,658 --> 00:47:08,492
OLIGODANG SECURED

1187
00:47:09,910 --> 00:47:12,162
Carbonated drinks would be good too.

1188
00:47:12,246 --> 00:47:13,330
Fanta?

1189
00:47:13,413 --> 00:47:14,456
We should taste them.

1190
00:47:14,540 --> 00:47:15,666
CARBONATED DRINK SECURED

1191
00:47:15,749 --> 00:47:17,084
JUN-HO JOINS AFTER CHANGING

1192
00:47:17,167 --> 00:47:18,001
Taste them?

1193
00:47:18,085 --> 00:47:19,920
We're supposed to make the welcome drinks.

1194
00:47:20,003 --> 00:47:21,838
ADDING OLIGODANG TO LEMON WATER

1195
00:47:21,922 --> 00:47:23,048
Should we add it in?

1196
00:47:26,843 --> 00:47:28,512
CURIOUS

1197
00:47:28,595 --> 00:47:30,222
It's… not delicious.

1198
00:47:33,559 --> 00:47:35,519
It really is not good.

1199
00:47:36,019 --> 00:47:37,229
Let's mix in a bit of Fanta.

1200
00:47:37,312 --> 00:47:41,441
LEMON WATER, OLIGODANG, SODA

1201
00:47:43,694 --> 00:47:46,947
It tastes like
they all made each other worse.

1202
00:47:51,285 --> 00:47:53,620
- You can taste all three of them.
- Right.

1203
00:47:57,249 --> 00:47:59,668
I think we should go back to square one.

1204
00:47:59,751 --> 00:48:01,003
SQUARE ONE?

1205
00:48:01,086 --> 00:48:02,838
Let's add a little bit of this to water.

1206
00:48:02,921 --> 00:48:05,173
Because lemon juice

1207
00:48:05,257 --> 00:48:06,758
is healthy for us.

1208
00:48:06,842 --> 00:48:08,343
About 30 drops.

1209
00:48:09,469 --> 00:48:10,929
- Two, three.
- Two, three.

1210
00:48:12,139 --> 00:48:14,224
Four, five, six,

1211
00:48:14,308 --> 00:48:16,101
seven, eight, nine.

1212
00:48:16,685 --> 00:48:17,978
Okay, I think that's enough.

1213
00:48:18,604 --> 00:48:20,230
The color's the same.

1214
00:48:23,025 --> 00:48:23,942
I like this.

1215
00:48:24,026 --> 00:48:24,860
- This one?
- Yes.

1216
00:48:24,943 --> 00:48:26,194
- I like this one too.
- Really?

1217
00:48:26,278 --> 00:48:27,821
- Yeah, 30.
- Let's make it 30 drops.

1218
00:48:27,904 --> 00:48:28,780
Exactly 30 drops.

1219
00:48:28,864 --> 00:48:29,948
THEY FOUND THE GOLDEN RATIO

1220
00:48:30,032 --> 00:48:31,116
Yeah, let's do that.

1221
00:48:31,199 --> 00:48:32,534
We'll do it when they come.

1222
00:48:32,618 --> 00:48:35,203
MEANWHILE, BOSS COOKS DINNER

1223
00:48:35,287 --> 00:48:36,538
I should make six pizzas.

1224
00:48:36,622 --> 00:48:38,540
TODAY'S DISH
6 KIMCHI CHEESE PIZZAS

1225
00:48:41,084 --> 00:48:44,129
SPECIAL TOPPING IS MEAT

1226
00:48:44,755 --> 00:48:46,923
- Jun-ho, can you help me cook the meat?
- Sure.

1227
00:48:47,007 --> 00:48:49,051
What else do you need help with?

1228
00:48:49,134 --> 00:48:51,011
I only need help with the meat.

1229
00:48:51,094 --> 00:48:51,928
Got it.

1230
00:48:52,012 --> 00:48:54,056
WHILE JUN-HO GRILLS THE MEAT

1231
00:48:54,139 --> 00:48:56,350
KIAN PREPS THE TOPPINGS

1232
00:48:59,144 --> 00:49:00,437
CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPERS?

1233
00:49:01,355 --> 00:49:03,273
I should make different spice levels.

1234
00:49:03,357 --> 00:49:06,943
Extreme, medium, and mild.

1235
00:49:07,819 --> 00:49:08,904
It's hot.

1236
00:49:09,613 --> 00:49:10,447
It's so hot.

1237
00:49:10,530 --> 00:49:11,573
- Right?
- Yeah.

1238
00:49:11,657 --> 00:49:13,617
5 CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPERS

1239
00:49:13,700 --> 00:49:14,951
8 CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPERS

1240
00:49:16,328 --> 00:49:18,330
ADDING 5 MORE

1241
00:49:19,247 --> 00:49:21,375
13 CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPERS SO FAR

1242
00:49:21,458 --> 00:49:22,501
More peppers.

1243
00:49:23,794 --> 00:49:25,420
ADDING 7 MORE

1244
00:49:26,380 --> 00:49:27,214
Gosh, it's spicy.

1245
00:49:31,385 --> 00:49:33,303
20 CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPERS PREPPED

1246
00:49:33,387 --> 00:49:34,221
Gosh, my back.

1247
00:49:35,055 --> 00:49:36,598
HE MAKES THE DOUGH RIGHT AWAY

1248
00:49:37,224 --> 00:49:38,642
It's my first time making pizza.

1249
00:49:40,435 --> 00:49:41,395
Geez.

1250
00:49:46,608 --> 00:49:48,026
You're even making dough.

1251
00:49:48,735 --> 00:49:50,320
Do you know how to make pizza dough?

1252
00:49:50,404 --> 00:49:52,155
It's all just flour in the end.

1253
00:49:53,782 --> 00:49:55,325
I thought there was a ratio.

1254
00:49:55,826 --> 00:49:56,952
- Ratio?
- Yeah.

1255
00:49:57,035 --> 00:49:58,620
I have no idea. I'm just going by feel.

1256
00:49:59,621 --> 00:50:01,164
They say beating it makes it better.

1257
00:50:05,877 --> 00:50:07,087
Become delicious.

1258
00:50:11,007 --> 00:50:12,843
You're literally beating it up.

1259
00:50:13,969 --> 00:50:14,803
Hand-beaten.

1260
00:50:15,303 --> 00:50:18,306
HAND-BEATEN DOUGH

1261
00:50:18,390 --> 00:50:19,474
All done.

1262
00:50:19,558 --> 00:50:23,520
Aren't you supposed to shape the dough
into a ball and let it rest?

1263
00:50:23,603 --> 00:50:24,438
Normally, yes.

1264
00:50:24,938 --> 00:50:27,566
But as I punched it, it already fermented.

1265
00:50:27,649 --> 00:50:29,651
DOUGH IS READY
AFTER FERMENTING IT WITH PUNCHES

1266
00:50:35,115 --> 00:50:36,491
Put oil in the pan.

1267
00:50:39,244 --> 00:50:41,163
ADDS MORE OIL

1268
00:50:41,913 --> 00:50:45,125
AND ADDS EVEN MORE

1269
00:50:45,709 --> 00:50:47,210
This one's big, so…

1270
00:50:47,794 --> 00:50:49,379
Why is it so sticky?

1271
00:50:52,048 --> 00:50:52,966
All right.

1272
00:50:54,009 --> 00:50:55,218
Be careful.

1273
00:50:55,302 --> 00:50:56,845
I didn't turn on the stove yet.

1274
00:50:57,429 --> 00:50:58,472
Spread it out.

1275
00:51:00,182 --> 00:51:01,475
It looks like a <i>hotteok</i><i></i>pancake.

1276
00:51:01,558 --> 00:51:02,851
Right?

1277
00:51:02,934 --> 00:51:04,102
Gosh, this is…

1278
00:51:04,186 --> 00:51:05,270
Shouldn't it be thinner?

1279
00:51:05,353 --> 00:51:06,688
It should, but…

1280
00:51:06,772 --> 00:51:09,483
NO MATTER HOW HARD HE TRIES

1281
00:51:09,566 --> 00:51:11,109
IT DOESN'T GET THINNER

1282
00:51:11,193 --> 00:51:12,652
Hey, this is… Hold on.

1283
00:51:12,736 --> 00:51:14,112
This is not right.

1284
00:51:15,947 --> 00:51:17,073
What do I do?

1285
00:51:17,783 --> 00:51:18,825
Why won't it spread out?

1286
00:51:18,909 --> 00:51:20,494
This is bad.

1287
00:51:23,163 --> 00:51:24,456
This is bad.

1288
00:51:25,874 --> 00:51:27,000
Damn it.

1289
00:51:27,083 --> 00:51:28,376
What are you doing?

1290
00:51:28,960 --> 00:51:30,295
Why won't it spread out?

1291
00:51:30,378 --> 00:51:32,672
FLUSTERED

1292
00:51:35,675 --> 00:51:37,010
I'll try to save this.

1293
00:51:37,093 --> 00:51:38,136
HE GRABS IT

1294
00:51:38,220 --> 00:51:41,348
With the oil, I think it'll work.

1295
00:51:41,431 --> 00:51:44,726
AFTER RUBBING OIL ON IT,
HE TRIES TO SPREAD IT OUT AGAIN

1296
00:51:44,810 --> 00:51:47,103
Hey, it's spreading out now.

1297
00:51:49,356 --> 00:51:50,524
- Is it?
- Yeah.

1298
00:51:50,607 --> 00:51:52,526
- I see.
- Wide like this.

1299
00:51:55,237 --> 00:51:57,572
SECOND PIZZA

1300
00:51:57,656 --> 00:51:58,907
This God damn thing.

1301
00:52:04,788 --> 00:52:07,040
Man, making pizza is so hard.

1302
00:52:07,123 --> 00:52:08,291
Of course.

1303
00:52:08,375 --> 00:52:10,126
I guess it does require skill.

1304
00:52:10,210 --> 00:52:11,878
I've always only made Korean food.

1305
00:52:12,462 --> 00:52:13,505
Nice and wide.

1306
00:52:13,588 --> 00:52:15,423
THIRD PIZZA

1307
00:52:15,507 --> 00:52:17,008
Make it wide.

1308
00:52:17,092 --> 00:52:19,094
Jun-ho, could you take some dough

1309
00:52:19,177 --> 00:52:20,804
- and try to make one?
- Sure.

1310
00:52:20,887 --> 00:52:22,347
I should try it too.

1311
00:52:26,268 --> 00:52:27,102
I think…

1312
00:52:27,185 --> 00:52:29,813
Yeah, we should use a rolling pin.

1313
00:52:29,896 --> 00:52:31,815
Then, you can toss it.

1314
00:52:32,524 --> 00:52:35,110
You're right. That's what I was missing.

1315
00:52:35,193 --> 00:52:36,778
I think you made the dough well.

1316
00:52:37,320 --> 00:52:38,738
- Not bad, right?
- Yeah.

1317
00:52:39,364 --> 00:52:41,533
I think you could toss it
if you stretched it out.

1318
00:52:44,744 --> 00:52:46,454
Gently like this.

1319
00:52:49,082 --> 00:52:50,333
It's getting wider.

1320
00:52:50,417 --> 00:52:51,501
Right?

1321
00:52:51,585 --> 00:52:52,794
Yeah.

1322
00:52:52,878 --> 00:52:54,921
- Good. It's gotten wider.
- It's gotten big.

1323
00:52:55,005 --> 00:52:57,340
Yeah. It gets pretty big.

1324
00:53:00,677 --> 00:53:01,636
Yes.

1325
00:53:03,680 --> 00:53:04,973
Why does mine

1326
00:53:05,056 --> 00:53:06,850
look like a mung bean pancake?

1327
00:53:11,396 --> 00:53:14,441
PUTTING TOMATO SAUCE
ON MUNG BEAN PANCAKE?

1328
00:53:14,524 --> 00:53:16,735
Gosh, I put in too much oil.

1329
00:53:18,194 --> 00:53:20,322
This will be the spiciest one.

1330
00:53:21,406 --> 00:53:22,699
Cheongyang chili pepper.

1331
00:53:24,576 --> 00:53:25,619
A bunch of it.

1332
00:53:25,702 --> 00:53:27,746
A LOT OF CHEONGYANG CHILI PEPPERS

1333
00:53:31,124 --> 00:53:34,502
SECOND PIZZA

1334
00:53:35,128 --> 00:53:37,714
A BUNCH OF CHILI PEPPERS AGAIN?

1335
00:53:38,214 --> 00:53:41,927
THIRD ONE HAS A LOT AS WELL

1336
00:53:42,010 --> 00:53:43,970
All three ended up as spicy ones.

1337
00:53:45,096 --> 00:53:46,097
It'll be all right.

1338
00:53:47,724 --> 00:53:50,852
AND A LOT OF OTHER TOPPINGS

1339
00:53:50,936 --> 00:53:53,897
BIG

1340
00:53:55,607 --> 00:53:59,152
MEANWHILE

1341
00:54:05,075 --> 00:54:09,746
JUN-HO CUTS HIS TOPPINGS
INTO BITE-SIZED PIECES

1342
00:54:09,829 --> 00:54:12,207
I like adding the chili peppers.

1343
00:54:12,290 --> 00:54:15,502
But our Japanese guest
might not be able to eat spicy food.

1344
00:54:15,585 --> 00:54:17,879
- That must be a basic one.
- Right, it is.

1345
00:54:17,963 --> 00:54:19,339
JUN-HO MAKES A MILD ONE

1346
00:54:21,675 --> 00:54:25,512
THE LAST TWO ARE MADE
WITH ONLY KIMCHI AND CHEESE

1347
00:54:28,556 --> 00:54:30,141
Adjusting the heat is key.

1348
00:54:30,225 --> 00:54:31,935
WAITING UNTIL THEY COOK

1349
00:54:32,018 --> 00:54:33,603
Weak enough not to burn it.

1350
00:54:34,187 --> 00:54:35,563
I think this is ready.

1351
00:54:36,481 --> 00:54:38,400
THEY CHECK IF IT COOKED WELL

1352
00:54:38,984 --> 00:54:40,151
Open it.

1353
00:54:46,491 --> 00:54:48,118
- It looks good now.
- Right?

1354
00:54:48,201 --> 00:54:49,452
- Yeah.
- It doesn't look too bad.

1355
00:54:49,536 --> 00:54:51,454
See if the dough's burnt.

1356
00:54:51,538 --> 00:54:52,872
Is it burnt or not?

1357
00:54:52,956 --> 00:54:53,957
Hey, it's…

1358
00:54:55,250 --> 00:54:57,711
It's become pretty crisp. Let's just…

1359
00:55:03,633 --> 00:55:05,093
Let's scrape it off.

1360
00:55:05,176 --> 00:55:06,678
Then, it'll be all right.

1361
00:55:06,761 --> 00:55:10,390
If we scrape it off
until we see the white part…

1362
00:55:12,475 --> 00:55:14,436
It's just like brick oven pizza, isn't it?

1363
00:55:14,519 --> 00:55:16,312
Brick oven, my foot.

1364
00:55:16,396 --> 00:55:17,439
Let's scrape it off.

1365
00:55:24,279 --> 00:55:25,321
What? Is it burnt?

1366
00:55:25,405 --> 00:55:26,573
What? No.

1367
00:55:26,656 --> 00:55:27,782
It's going well.

1368
00:55:27,866 --> 00:55:29,367
We can just get rid of this.

1369
00:55:32,245 --> 00:55:33,747
- Damn it.
- Is there a problem?

1370
00:55:33,830 --> 00:55:34,664
Damn it.

1371
00:55:34,748 --> 00:55:37,042
KIAN'S BIZARRE B&B SEASON 2

1372
00:56:22,796 --> 00:56:24,798
Subtitle translation by: Wayne Ryu
